}

^["recursive_improvement"]{
 loop: [
  "? before a move, grep every invoker: npm names, hooks, skills, agent commands, docs, plan touches",
  "< move one script or cluster per commit, leaving a shim where anything external invokes it",
  "$ record which names still route through a shim",
  "^ fold canonical names back into CLAUDE.md, skills, and docs in the same pass",
  "% keep the commit gate and spw init consumer hooks working at every commit",
 ]
 gates: [#hooks_green, #consumer_hooks_green, #index_check_green]
}

^["risk_model"]{
 hard_failures: [
  "the commit gate or a consumer hook sources a moved script and stops reviewing",
  "a rename leaves the allowlisted prefixes, so agents start prompting or stop running checks"
 ]
 soft_failures: [
  "skills and docs cite an old name for a release",
  "a reintegrated verb prints different output than the script it replaced"
 ]
 non_negotiables: [
  "spw-syntax-review.ts and poll-review.sh keep working for consumer hooks; they become shims, never vanish",
  "no destructive script runs with a built-in force flag",
  "every removal names its replacement in the warning it printed first"
 ]
}

^["validation"]{
 hypotheses: [
  "H1 test:all exposes the 3 analyzer and 2 smoke failures that test:run hides today",
  "H2 every npm name that survives describes what it runs",
  "H3 the reintegrated verbs reproduce the scripts' outputs on one fixture set"
 ]
 negative_controls: [
  "spw-init-portability.test.ts passes at every commit",
  "a staged commit runs the same gate review before and after"
 ]
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-10-13 12:40] observe — A read-only review of every audit and tooling script found a hazard: spw:reset runs git clean on .spw with force built in, and the local allowlist admits spw npm scripts without a prompt. It also found hidden failures: test:analyzers fails 3 of 34 and lsp:smoke 2 of 22, and neither runs in test:run. And it found breakage: the source bundle omits packages, the poll-review fuzz flags are inert, and the gate still checks a lib/spw that does not exist. Details, per script, in the artifact.
 >>[2026-10-13 12:40] decide — This plan absorbs audit-fuzz-truthfulness retire_alias_profiles and hygiene-index-consolidation npm_scripts_canonical as ~[truthful_aliases]; the spw plan and agent verbs coordinate with plan-tooling-design; the scripts adapter for version control stays with local-numbering-vcs.
 >>[2026-10-13 17:16] implement — Landed cdbb6912: npm run spw:reset previews what it would discard and exits 1; only bash scripts/spw-reset.sh --force discards, and the dev.ts hint names the forced script. A probe file in .spw survived the npm script. lint:spw:strict, test:all, and the source bundle move to suite_and_bundle. resolved [reset_fate].
}

^["open"]{
 ?[hook_install]: "Hooks are copied into .git/hooks by hand; does an install-hooks step land here, or with the commit gate's own plan?"
 ?[spw_review_shape]: "Is the review cluster one spw review verb with --parse and --landscape, as conventions/cli.spw plans, or two verbs?"
}

^["commits"]{
 ~[plan]: ".[plans] — tooling-scripts-consolidation records the scripts review and its commit sequence"
 .[safe_reset](cdbb6912): "#[scripts] — npm run spw:reset only previews; discarding .spw work takes bash scripts/spw-reset.sh --force"
 ~[suite_and_bundle]: "#[scripts] — lint:spw:strict and test:all exist, and srcdist bundles packages; split from safe_reset, which landed the reset alone"
 ~[pin_analyzers]: "![analyzers] — topography and refactor-check tests match current parse health, and test:analyzers joins the headless suite"
 ~[gate_dead_checks]: "&[commit-gate] — run-review drops the lib/spw boundary check and the ~# warning, and poll-review fuzz flags either reach eslint or go"
 ~[truthful_aliases]: "vocab[scripts] — fuzz:complexity, dead, naming, async, and boonhonk, analyze:patterns, lint:changed, and the compat spw names warn and route to truthful names (from audit-fuzz-truthfulness retire_alias_profiles and hygiene-index-consolidation npm_scripts_canonical)"
 ~[docs_truth]: ".[docs] — CLAUDE.md, skills, agent commands, and docs/contributing cite canonical names; lint:layers and lint:fix cites are resolved"
 ~[lsp_shims]: "&[lsp] — npm run lsp runs the package bridge, the re-export shims go, and smoke-navigation moves into packages/spw-lsp"
 ~[archive_check]: "&[analyzers] — the three v020 checks and runtime-filename become one archive-contract-check behind the lint:v020 names"
 ~[verbs_absorb]: "&[cli] — spw resolve, delta --ast, form, and lint --particles absorb path-check, refactor-check, topography and flow, and particle census, with the npm names routed"
 ~[spw_review]: "&[cli] — spw review reads seed syntax-stack as the only profile source, and spw-syntax-review.ts stays as a shim for consumer hooks"
 ~[spw_plan_verbs]: "&[plans] — spw plan and spw agent own init, stream, status, check, index, kb, and vibe; agent-tools.sh dispatches to them; kb stops printing absolute paths; card touches follow"
 ~[retire_ui]: "&[audit] — ui-contract-audit, perturbation-scan, and the UI-era skill loaders warn, and audit-full drops the UI checks"
}

